WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.980
It has been said that one is the loneliest
number that you will ever know.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.880
But at least the number one is a number that
can actually be known.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.590
What could we possibly mean by that?

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:15.711
Well, try to imagine a number that cannot
possibly be known or quantified, a missing

00:00:15.711 --> 00:00:17.590
number if you will.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:19.439
No, not that one.

00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:24.480
This is a number that you can never put into
an equation or a formula, and it does not

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.669
appear in the numerical sequence.

00:00:26.669 --> 00:00:33.160
You cannot count to it, add to, divide, or
multiply by it, or even see it, and yet this

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.220
number still somehow exists.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.190
Sounds impossible, doesn’t it?

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:43.150
After all, the mathematicians among you will
understand that numbers are not a force of

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:44.150
nature.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:48.440
They aren’t a metaphysical aspect of our
reality like space or time.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:53.490
Numbers are a tool, in a way, a tool created
by human beings.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:58.570
We use them to measure and calculate, numbers
help us make some sense of the crazy world

00:00:58.570 --> 00:00:59.850
that we all live in.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:05.460
Just ask your math teacher and they’ll tell
you how important numbers are to human civilization!

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:12.030
The point is, ancient mathematicians invented
numbers, so how could a number ever be missing?

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.100
What makes a number unknowable?

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.969
Well, perhaps it’s time you learned.

00:01:16.969 --> 00:01:24.009
Math class is in session and today, we’re
talking about SCP-033, also known by the appropriate

00:01:24.009 --> 00:01:26.799
nickname of “The Missing Number.”

00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:31.581
As you may have already gathered, the whole
point of SCP-033 is that it can’t be fully

00:01:31.581 --> 00:01:34.539
understood by the ordinary human mind.

00:01:34.539 --> 00:01:39.179
Even highly trained mathematicians, experts
in the use of numbers able to understand the

00:01:39.179 --> 00:01:44.119
most complex equations, are barely able to
interpret the formula that results in this

00:01:44.119 --> 00:01:45.319
Missing Number.

00:01:45.319 --> 00:01:50.039
At present, it exists written down on an irregularly
shaped piece of paper.

00:01:50.039 --> 00:01:54.619
This paper does not have any right angles,
no parallel borders and the length of each

00:01:54.619 --> 00:01:57.350
side is different from all others.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:02.929
The SCP Foundation keeps this paper stored
securely, locked up at the minimum safe distance

00:02:02.929 --> 00:02:07.789
of thirty meters away from any computer or
other electronic devices.

00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:13.420
On the paper itself is the mathematical formula
that equals SCP-033.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:18.069
As you can probably imagine, the formula is
intensely complex.

00:02:18.069 --> 00:02:22.040
It is filled with mathematical symbols ranging
from common ones that you would immediately

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:28.930
recognize, to those that are way more sophisticated
and would likely require a PhD to fully understand.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:33.349
And then there are parts of this unfathomable
problem that would baffle even the world’s

00:02:33.349 --> 00:02:35.329
most notable math geniuses.

00:02:35.329 --> 00:02:40.010
But, all of these symbols and numbers coalesce
to equal a number that has somehow been missed

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:44.940
by all of humanity, throughout the entire
history of our civilization.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:49.730
One noted mathematician by the name of Professor
Hutchinson, who first observed the calculation

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:54.350
of SCP-033, referred to The Missing Number
as Θ′

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:59.390
Okay, so here we have a number that can barely
be understood by the average person, created

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:04.430
by a formula so complex that when written
down it might as well be a page full of gibberish.

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:08.019
Surely there couldn’t be anything more to
it than that, right?

00:03:08.019 --> 00:03:12.219
Wrong, you should know by now that the SCP
Foundation doesn’t concern themselves with

00:03:12.219 --> 00:03:15.390
the mundane, ordinary type of strange.

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:20.790
They deal exclusively in the kind of strange
that has anomalous origins and properties.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:26.319
In the case of SCP-033, the Missing Number
is so complex that it practically breaks every

00:03:26.319 --> 00:03:28.920
and all rules of mathematics.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:33.950
In other words, Theta Prime cannot possibly
remain fixed within our reality.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:38.750
The reason why the paper Theta Prime is written
on has to have such unusual dimensions is

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.459
due to the anomalous effect of the number.

00:03:41.459 --> 00:03:46.220
When written onto ordinary paper, canvas,
or any other similar surface or material,

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:49.760
The Missing Number will begin to break down
whatever it has been written on.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:54.540
It will literally erode and disintegrate anything
on a molecular level.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:58.230
You might be forgiven for thinking you could
get around that by typing out the equation

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:02.200
for Theta Prime on a computer, but you would
be wrong.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:07.159
This reaction even affects technology, burning
out any and all devices someone attempts to

00:04:07.159 --> 00:04:10.370
digitally store SCP-033 on.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:12.340
And if written on literally anything else?

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:17.199
Well, then the Missing Number will fade, become
obscured and unintelligible in a matter of

00:04:17.199 --> 00:04:19.639
seconds, unreadable to anyone.

00:04:19.639 --> 00:04:25.340
We’ve talked a lot about what SCP-033 does,
mainly because we can’t really show or tell

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:26.870
you what it looks like.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:30.680
Well, unless you want your computer, phone,
or tablet to break down and melt from the

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.020
inside-out.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:36.979
Like we mentioned earlier, Theta Prime cannot
remain fixed in our reality, and it will fade

00:04:36.979 --> 00:04:41.970
away from any surface or destroy any devices
used to display or calculate it.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:46.310
But the anomalous effects of the Missing Number
do not stop there.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:51.650
SCP-033 also possesses the ability to “leap”
from any safe material, like the paper of

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.759
specific dimensions that it is written and
stored on.

00:04:54.759 --> 00:04:58.960
This is why the safe containing the paper
with the Missing Number equations written

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:04.620
on it has to be kept a certain distance away
from any electronic devices, or other surfaces

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:06.880
that can display Theta Prime.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:14.150
Should a material safely storing SCP-033 come
into contact with anything unsafe, say a computer,

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:18.900
then the Missing Number will pass onto the
unsafe device, material or surface and begin

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.800
to destabilize its atomic structure.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:27.449
Any paper or electronic storage device within
a thirty meter safe distance of SCP-033 risks

00:05:27.449 --> 00:05:33.750
becoming a victim of Theta Prime, almost as
if the number itself is an infectious virus.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:38.600
Although the SCP Foundation’s top researchers
have tried their best to find one, there currently

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:42.770
exists no safe way to store SCP-033 digitally.

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:47.050
The Foundation has a number of projects that
are still ongoing, looking into the best possible

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:52.800
method to store the Missing Number electronically,
without posing a risk to their computer systems.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:57.860
Additionally, the Foundation has long been
conducting research of a different nature:

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:00.740
Trying to find some way of weaponizing SCP-033.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:04.640
It doesn’t seem like a bad idea, right?

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:08.789
After all, Theta Prime functions a lot like
a computer virus when it comes into contact

00:06:08.789 --> 00:06:12.590
with machines, so why wouldn’t they try
to use it as a weapon?

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:16.781
It is the goal of these projects, that the
Foundation will be able to use the Missing

00:06:16.781 --> 00:06:21.169
Number as a way to neutralize hostile, machine
SCPs.

00:06:21.169 --> 00:06:25.830
Any anomalies that they encounter that operate
on logic based systems, such as artificial

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:32.460
intelligences, could in theory be susceptible
to the destructive effects of SCP-033.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:36.789
Within the SCP Archive file for the Missing
Number, is a classified article that details

00:06:36.789 --> 00:06:43.080
more about the discovery of SCP-033, before
going on to explore the results of the Foundation’s

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:47.099
testing with Theta Prime’s use as a cyber
weapon of sorts.

00:06:47.099 --> 00:06:51.280
First and foremost is a transcript from a
debriefing with Professor Hutchinson.

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:55.169
If you were paying attention earlier, then
you will remember that this is the same Professor

00:06:55.169 --> 00:07:02.180
Hutchinson that first observed SCP-033, and
as a noted mathematician, he has some invaluable

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:06.470
inside knowledge on the nature of Theta Prime,
as he calls it.

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:09.640
“Every school child knows that 2 plus 2
is 4.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:14.840
The solid mathematical certainty of numerical
order and value is the basis for all logic-based

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:15.840
systems.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:19.160
We know that after 2 comes 3 and after 3 comes
4.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:23.069
What this formula proves is that we missed
a number somewhere.

00:07:23.069 --> 00:07:27.630
Imagine if all of our technology was based
on the belief that after 4 came 6.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:31.509
We simply didn't know or conceive of 5.

00:07:31.509 --> 00:07:35.539
That is, in essence, what this formula proves—we
missed a number.”

00:07:35.539 --> 00:07:40.340
The Professor then goes on to ponder why hand
crafted vellum works the best for containing

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:42.550
SCP-033.

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:46.370
Vellum is essentially an older type of fine
parchment that originally would have been

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:49.770
made from the skin of a calf or other young
animal.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:53.919
Professor Hutchinson seems to theorize that
there are two ways this particular material

00:07:53.919 --> 00:07:57.520
is able to keep SCP-033 written on it.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:02.319
“One, the irregularity of the crafting process
due to human error serves to eliminate any

00:08:02.319 --> 00:08:06.500
traces of regularity that would be found in
a machine-created product.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:11.550
Two, the irregular borders seem to confuse
it somehow, as if it gets locked up looking

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:14.979
for a pattern to identify and use as an escape
hatch.

00:08:14.979 --> 00:08:19.789
I'll tell you this, though, I don't think
it should be left on anything longer than

00:08:19.789 --> 00:08:21.250
a few days.

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:22.880
It will find a pattern eventually.”

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:27.419
Finally, Professor Hutchinson then goes on
to talk about the anomalous effects of the

00:08:27.419 --> 00:08:32.130
Missing Number, specifically its ability to
destroy materials or computers that it comes

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:33.719
into contact with.

00:08:33.719 --> 00:08:38.860
Hutchinson posits the theory that Theta Prime
does not actually destroy anything, but instead

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:42.979
tries to integrate itself into a system or
onto a page.

00:08:42.979 --> 00:08:47.970
But the system or page cannot cope with the
Missing Number, and so breaks down.

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:53.490
It is almost as if he thinks the number itself
wants to be understood, it longs for humanity

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:58.680
to understand it after having been missed
for so very, very long.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:04.200
But Theta Prime is so utterly beyond our understanding
that it has the potentially to be devastating.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:09.480
“It’s like trying to cram another book
into a completely full bookshelf.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:14.680
If you get a hammer, you can get it in there,
but the whole shelf bursts eventually.

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:19.810
If it gets out into the internet, we will
potentially experience a full IT infrastructure

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:21.500
collapse within hours.”

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:27.050
During one of their numerous tests with SCP-033,
the Foundation’s researchers wrote the various

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:32.430
equations and formulae that equal Theta Prime
on a standard piece of white copy paper, referred

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:33.650
to as X1.

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:39.310
Then, they placed a second sheet, X2, just
thirty centimeters away from X1.

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:43.660
Within about a minute, the same mathematical
symbols and formulae on X1 had started to

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:45.720
appear on X2.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:50.450
After one hundred and sixty seconds, the second
page was full with the complete equation for

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:51.950
the Missing Number.

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:57.920
After around five minutes, both X1 and X2
began to appear slightly damp, however Theta

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:02.300
Prime and its related equations were still
visible on the pages.

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:06.960
After double that time, the first page, X1,
had begun to separate, dissolving partly into

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:10.240
water and the rest into the pulp that had
formed the paper itself.

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:15.610
While it still kept the same standard shape
and size, the formulae written on it had since

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:16.920
become unreadable.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:22.100
X2 was still wet as well, but SCP-033 was
still visible.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:26.620
After over twenty-one minutes had passed,
X1 had been completely destroyed.

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:31.370
The water component of it had evaporated,
and the paper pulp had also disappeared.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:36.300
The second page, X2, soon followed the exact
same process of being structurally broken

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:41.440
down and unmade atom by atom until there was
nothing left.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:45.230
It becomes terrifying to think what might
happen if you wrote the equations for the

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:48.240
Missing Number on another human being.

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:52.290
While their testing has yet to produce any
tangible results, the Foundation’s staff

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:56.670
always make sure they transfer the Missing
Number onto a whiteboard or chalkboard whenever

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:57.880
studying it.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:03.330
Upon doing so, researchers are instructed
to incinerate the paper that SCP-033 was written

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:07.930
on previously, preventing multiple instances
of Theta Prime and hopefully stopping the

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:10.389
number from spreading further.

00:11:10.389 --> 00:11:16.470
Any researchers observing or experimenting
with SCP-033 must do so within a safe distance,

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:19.800
away from computers and other devices.

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:23.920
Testing can only occur for a maximum of 42
minutes before the Missing Number will destroy

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:27.420
the surface it is written on, or fade from
view.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:32.350
While dangerous, volatile, and potentially
hugely destructive if it ever fell into the

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:37.160
wrong hands, Theta Prime is a strangely insightful
SCP.

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:41.399
Knowing there exists a Missing Number must
be similar to how mathematicians felt about

00:11:41.399 --> 00:11:43.510
the introduction of variables.

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:47.690
You will probably have seen these a lot in
your algebra homework, ‘find the value of

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:49.339
x’ and so on.

00:11:49.339 --> 00:11:55.490
Like SCP-033, that is also a number that cannot
fully ‘exist’ in our reality unless you

00:11:55.490 --> 00:11:57.200
figure out its value.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:01.800
It influences the calculations you have to
make to find it, but it cannot be seen or

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:04.160
understood fully at first.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:08.149
Perhaps there will come a day when we can
store the missing number properly.

00:12:08.149 --> 00:12:14.269
But until then, we can only hope it never
finds its way into our favorite notebook...

00:12:14.269 --> 00:12:21.139
Now go check out “SCP-1861 - The Crew of
the HMS Wintersheimer” and “SCP-823 - Carnival

00:12:21.139 --> 00:12:24.040
of Horrors” for more SCPs that’ll blow
your mind!

